2. FREE PRODUCTION USE (UP TO TWO SEATS ON FOUR DEVICES)
You may use the Software in production free of charge provided that your total
number of Seats does not exceed two (2) and your total number of Devices does not
exceed four (4). Both limits apply; exceeding either one ends the free allowance.

3. COMMERCIAL LICENSE REQUIRED ABOVE THOSE LIMITS
Any production use of the Software that exceeds two (2) Seats or four (4) Devices
requires a paid commercial license from the Licensor, granted on a per-Seat basis.
A commercial license places no limit on Devices. See COMMERCIAL.md for how to
obtain one.

4. REDISTRIBUTION
You may redistribute the Software or derivative works provided that you (a) retain
this license text, the copyright notice, and all notices; and (b) do not remove,
weaken, or circumvent the Seat or Device limitations. Any recipient receives the Software
under this same license, with the same rights and the same limitations.

5. ATTRIBUTION (NOTICE)
If you deploy or redistribute the Software (including running it to coordinate or
orchestrate work, whether or not you redistribute its source), you must include a
file named FERRYMAN.md in the root of the source repository or distribution of any
project that uses the Software, stating that the project uses Ferryman and linking
to the Software's repository and this license. Text substantially as follows
satisfies this requirement:

    This project uses Ferryman (https://github.com/estejosh/ferryman),
    licensed under the Ferryman Source-Available License.

This requirement does not apply to individual end users who merely interact with
the outputs of a project that uses the Software; it applies to the party that
deploys or redistributes the Software. It is separate from, and in addition to,
the notice-retention requirement in Section 4. The standard Ferryman setup tooling
writes this FERRYMAN.md automatically.

